-- Sets severity on the 16 transmission faults still NULL after the round-2 gearbox-fault
-- cleanup (20261012202224_gearbox_fault_cleanup_round2_comparisons_and_cost_text.sql). Values are
-- Martin-reviewed (critical/moderate/minor), e.g. MQ250's DMF wear is 'moderate' -- a wear item,
-- not a critical failure (the one row that WAS critical on MQ250, a near-duplicate DMF claim
-- about ARL/BAM petrol engines, was deleted in round 2 as intentional, not an oversight).
--
-- Generated by scripts/fill/write-gearbox-severity-migration.mjs. Every UPDATE is guarded on
-- id + exact text + severity IS NULL, so it can never overwrite a severity someone already
-- set by hand -- a row that's already been assigned a (possibly different) severity is left
-- untouched, not silently overridden.
--
-- Review-only: NOT run by this session. Expected postcondition after running: 0 transmission
-- faults with NULL severity, 24 rows total.
--
-- Depends on 20261012202224_gearbox_fault_cleanup_round2_comparisons_and_cost_text.sql having
-- already run: the VW DQ500 row below is matched by its POST-round-2 text ("Mechatronics
-- failure at very high mileage, repair ~1,200–2,000 EUR"), since round 2 is what produces
-- that text. Run strictly after round 2, same as the migration filename/timestamp order implies.

BEGIN;

-- VW DQ200
UPDATE catalog_component_faults
SET severity = 'minor'
WHERE id = '3892ca64-5110-479c-85ae-af68ec97cc72'::uuid AND lower(fault) = lower('Input shaft bearing noise in neutral') AND severity IS NULL;
